

                   ADVENTURER-KINGS:  GAME 3, TURN 9

                                  FOR

                                II KAHN







          Lorenzo Cammoranesi
          
              
                              




  Quote of the Week:

  Imperial Motto of Frederick III (1415-1493), Holy Roman Emperor and ruler 
of Austria:
  "The whole world is subject to Austria"


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  With the coming of the spring season Kahn set out to quench his thirst for 
glory.  He cast a Flood spell and Quantara Roo was magically flooded.

  A great host of warriors carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) into the Forest province of Gnarlia, 
held by II Kahn.  Odysseus (#97)'s forces took Gnarlia without any major 
engagements.  Odysseus leads approximately 2 Bowmen, 2 Dragons, 2 Eagles and 1
Trolls.
  With the coming of the early summer season, Kahn boldly marched his forces 
into Bir Nzaran (#1203).

  Soldiers bearing the battle-standards of the Uga-Buga Makumb (#1)ian 
empire marched on the Forest province of Peachwood, a land garrisoned by the 
soldiers of II Kahn.  Odysseus (#97)'s forces experienced little resistance 
in Peachwood and Odysseus there established our reign.  Odysseus leads 
approximately 1 Bowmen, 3 Dragons and 2 Eagles.

  II Kahn's forces initiated a campaign of conquest directed at Bir Nzaran, 
a Desert province owing allegiance to Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll 
(#1).  Kahn commanded the invading armies.  The defenders were led by the 
provincial garrison commander.  The armies were drawn up into lines of 
battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Bir Nzaran (1203):

            188th   
            Bowmen  
