  DEFENDING ARMY

  Odysseus led a host of loyal soldiers.  Hawkins led his armies into the 
battle.
  Odysseus was not very lucky this time, because a strong wind blew into his 
men's faces, giving Hawkins's men a small edge.  Further, his careful 
tactical plans did not succeed against Hawkins's clever counterstrokes, and 
his men entered battle with a slight tactical disadvantage.

  On the right wing, the Crack 334th Bowmen were arrayed against the Green 
63rd Legion.  The 206th Dragons soared over the 63rd Legion and attacked 
them.  The 334th Bowmen fought the 63rd Legion and smashed their skulls as 
if they were eggplants.
  In the interior front, the Veteran 198th Trolls faced the 52nd Bowmen.  
The 91st Dragons soared over the 52nd Bowmen and attacked without mercy.  
The 91st Dragons were decimated by the bolts loosed by the dangerous Bowmen. 
The 102nd Eagles were bothered by the fire of their feared Bowmen nemesis.  
In this match, the 198th Trolls obtained the upper hand when they ordered 
their trumpeters to disrupt the signals of their enemy.
  The ongoing struggle went on with a murderous fury.  A captain of the 52nd 
Bowmen perceived an opening in the enemy lines which had opened when they 
skirted a large rock outcropping.  By charging into the gap, the 52nd Bowmen 
gained a considerable advantage.  In spite of the 52nd Bowmen's good 
fortune, the 198th Trolls fought the 52nd Bowmen and overpowered them with 
their thundering charge.
  Out on the left wing, the Veteran 333rd Bowmen were arrayed against the 
68th Bowmen.  The 249th Dragons soared over the 68th Bowmen and attacked 
without mercy.  The 249th Dragons were decimated by the bolts fired by the 
pesky Bowmen.  In this match, the 333rd Bowmen's commander released a herd 
of pink-painted elephants to make his opponents believe they were going 
insane, but the ruse had little effect except to amuse them.  The 333rd 
Bowmen fought the 68th Bowmen and advanced at will.
  Odysseus's great horde overpowered the army of Kahn and took the field, 
scattering their enemies.  The 334th Bowmen scattered the 63rd Legion in all 
directions.  The 198th Trolls destroyed the 52nd Bowmen.  The 333rd Bowmen 
annihilated the 68th Bowmen.
  Odysseus's host ended the campaign successfully and conquered Bronzeleaf.  
His forces completely dispersed, Hawkins fled frightened and alone to Bir 
Nzaran.
  With the advent of the fall season Hawkins attempted an illegal move.  He 
tried to move from Bir Nzaran to Sherwood, a non-adjacent province.  
Instead, Hawkins journeyed to Peachwood.
  Talking to some friendly locals, Hawkins heard a rumor about a Catacombs 
in Abu Matariq (#106), occupied by the Hydra.  They maintain that the Hydra 
owns the Handbook of Swordsmanship.
  The fall season cooled into early winter.  Hawkins travelled to Sherwood.

  Thy humble servant,   Frodo, Squire to Hawkins


From: Charious
To: Kahn

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season, I set out to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I was magically killed by a dark Necromantic spell!  And so it 
came to pass that I met my tragic end.

  Thy humble servant,   Charious


