GENERAL INTELLIGENCE REPORT

Kingdom of Uga-Buga Makumb (#1):
  In spring, Quantara Roo was magically flooded.
  In early summer, the acting commander's soldiers, ill-supplied in the 
tortuous desert, suffered from thirst.
  Out on the right wing, the Veteran 220th Light Cavalry faced the 133rd 
Garrison.  On this field, the craven fear of a single soldier worked against 
the 133rd Garrison.  They were thrown into disarray when he ran, shouting 
"We're all cooked!"  The 220th Light Cavalry fought the 133rd Garrison and 
advanced at will.
  Out on the left outside flank, the Veteran 218th Legion were blessed by a 
band of priests sent by the League of Pagan Clerics, which inspired them to 
a fanatical zeal.  They were arrayed against the 166th Garrison.  The 188th 
Bowmen flanked the enemy and attacked with full force.  The 218th Legion 
fought the 166th Garrison and smashed their heads as if they were eggplants. 
The acting commander withdrew to the Callisto Sea.
  In fall, Guerin (#18) conducted military exercises and the 124th Skeletal 
Dragons improved in quality.
  In early summer, Odysseus (#97) rode his flying armies over to Peachwood.
  In late summer, Odysseus rode his flying armies into Bronzeleaf.
  In fall, Quantara Roo was hit by a plague.

  In early winter, Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) sent an invasion 
force into the adjacent Forest province of Maplehaven, owned by 
Giovanna d'Arco (#7).  Alaric (#22)'s forces conquered Maplehaven without 
any major engagements.


Kingdom of Giovanna d'Arco (#7):
  In spring, Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) sent an invasion force 
into the adjacent Forest province of Maplehaven, owned by Giovanna d'Arco 
(#7).  Alaric (#22)'s forces conquered Maplehaven without any major 
engagements.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have attained skill level 5 in Meleeing.  At levels 5
and up, the usual 10% per level increase in the chance to hit in melee is 
discontinued, as well as the damage plus (however, skill level will still 
determine who attacks first in combat).  Instead, your characters of this 
exalted level are awarded the following Advanced Ability: 
  MELEE- EVASION:  A character becomes expert at evading opponents when 
using the Flee tactic.  Slow opponents can always be evaded, Medium-speed 
opponents can be evaded 20% of the time, and Fast opponents are evaded 50% 
of the time.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  Your kingdom has attained skill level 5 in White Magic.  
At levels 5 and up, the usual 15% per level increase in the cast chance is 
discontinued, and the number of spells you can cast in White Magic is capped 
at 3 Action, 2 Combat.  The effects of the "Holy Symbol" and "Spiritwrack" 
spells are also capped at level 4 (however, skill level will still determine 
who attacks first in personal combat).  Instead, your characters of this 
high level are awarded a new Advanced Ability: 
  WHITE MAGIC- ENHANCED HOLY SYMBOL:  The Holy Symbol spell now has the same 
effect against opponents who have an Evil alignment as it does against 
Undead creatures.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have attained skill level 6 in White Magic.  Your 
characters of this high level are awarded a new Advanced Ability: 
  WHITE MAGIC- PLACES OF POWER:  The White Magician can now use the magic of 
certain Holy Places of Power to increase the success chance of spells.  At 
any Monastery, Altar or Great Hall, the success chance to cast a White Magic 
spell is increased by 20%.  For Search actions, the 20% bonus is applied 
when that type of feature is searched.  For Action spells, the bonus is 
applied if that feature type is in the same province as the character, and 
is not occupied by a monster.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have reached skill level 7 in White Magic.  All 
characters of this exalted level are awarded a new Advanced Ability: 
  WHITE MAGIC- "WORDS OF HEALING" SPELL (abbreviated "WH"):  A new Combat 
Spell is gained called "Words of Healing".  With this spell, a White 
Magician is able to heal himself even in the heat of battle (before now, 
healing required time-consuming magic rituals unusable in combat 
situations).  The character is completely healed when the Words of Healing 
are spoken, gaining back all lost hit points.  The spell is also half as 
likely to be disrupted by your opponent's tactics as other spells.  Note: 
with old Saga programs, order this spell with "GI 26".


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have attained level 8 in White Magic.  All 
characters of this high level are awarded the following Advanced Ability: 
  WHITE MAGIC- "KNOW ALIGNMENT" TALENT:  This special White Magic Talent 
constantly operates by itself, without having to cast a spell.  Whenever 
another character or monster is encountered, his exact alignment will 
immediately become apparent, as soon as the encounter or Search action is 
initiated.  A temper estimate will also be made.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  Your kingdom has attained skill level 9 in White Magic.  
Your characters of this high level are awarded the following Advanced 
Ability: 
  WHITE MAGIC- ENHANCED RESURRECTION:  A resurrected character becomes the 
same alignment as the spellcaster's king.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  Your kingdom has attained skill level 5 in Necromancy.  
At levels 5 and up, the usual 15% per level increase in the cast chance is 
discontinued, and the number of spells you can cast in Necromancy is capped 
at 3 Action, 2 Combat.  The effects of the "Skeletal Armies", "Plague" and 
"Hand of Death" spells are also capped at level 4 (however, skill level will 
still determine who attacks first in personal combat).  Instead, all 
characters of this high level gain the following Advanced Ability: 
  NECROMANCY- "GATE DEMON" SPELL (abbreviated "GD"):  By the dark power of 
this spell, an extra-dimensional gate is opened to the nether worlds, from 
where a demon is summoned to fight in place of the spellcaster.  The caster 
has no control over what type of demon will appear.  If the Demon wins, it 
will return to the Abyss from whence it came.  If it loses, the caster must 
continue the fight at the current combat range.  If another Mirror Image or 
Gate Demon spell is cast against it, both spells will be nullified.  A Demon 
may refuse to fight an opponent of Evil to Undead alignment (50% chance).  
Note: with old Saga programs, order this spell with "GI 28".


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have attained skill level 5 in Element Magic.  At 
levels 5 and up, the usual 15% per level increase in the cast chance is 
discontinued, and the number of spells you can cast in Element Magic is 
capped at 3 Action, 2 Combat.  The effects of the "Tornadoes", "Fireball" 
and "Ice Suspension" spells are also capped at level 4 (however, skill level 
will still determine who attacks first in personal combat).   Instead, your 
characters of this high level gain a new Advanced Ability: 
  ELEMENTAL MAGIC- PLACES OF POWER:  The Elemental Mage is now able to use 
the magic of certain Elemental Places of Power to increase the success 
chance of spells.  At any Sacred Rock, Mountain Peak or Ancient Megaliths, 
the success chance to cast an Elemental Magic spell is increased by 20%.  
For Search actions, the 20% bonus is applied when that type of feature is 
searched.  For Action spells, the bonus is applied if that feature type is 
in the same province as the character, and is not occupied by a monster.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have attained level 6 in Element Magic.  All 
characters of this high level gain the following Advanced Ability: 
  ELEMENTAL MAGIC- "LAVA POOL" SPELL (abbreviated "LP"):  The "Lava Pool of 
Fiery Death" spell enables the Elemental Mage to call upon the elemental 
spirits of Fire and Earth to cause the magma beneath the earth's surface to 
rise up and break apart the earth beneath the victim, who is sucked into a 
fiery whirlpool of death and sucked down into the very bowels of the earth.  
The spell won't work against flying, underwater, ghostly or anti-holy 
monsters, and there is usually a chance to escape it (30% chance for 
medium-speed opponents, 60% for fast opponents).  Note: with old Saga 
programs, order this spell with "GI 30".


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have reached level 7 in Element Magic.  Your 
characters of this high level gain a new Advanced Ability: 
  ELEMENTAL- ENHANCED EARTHQUAKE:  When an Earthquake is cast on a Sea 
province, the upheaval on the ocean floor creates a humongous tidal wave.  
Every military unit in the province has a 5% chance per level of the 
spellcaster of being destroyed (except for Whales and Mermen, who just dive 
under the wave).  The tidal wave will continue on, moving generally in the 
opposite direction from the spellcaster, destroying units in sea provinces 
as it moves along (but weakening by 5% upon entering each new province).  
When it finally hits a land province, it will end there, but will be 
effective against Fleets, Mermen and Whales (only) in that province, as they 
are washed ashore and beached.  If the wave hits the Ice Cap, it simply ends 
there.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  Your kingdom has reached level 8 in Element Magic.  Your 
characters of this exalted level gain a new Advanced Ability: 
  ELEMENTAL MAGIC- ENHANCED COMBAT SPELLS:  The "Fireball" and "Ice 
Suspension" spells are enhanced.  They are now strong enough that Fireball 
can be cast against underwater monsters, and Ice Suspension will work 
against any monster.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have attained level 9 in Element Magic.  Your 
characters of this exalted level gain the following Advanced Ability: 
  ELEMENTAL MAGIC- "MAKE GEMS" TALENT:  Using this Elemental Talent, each 
time the mage practices elemental ability (PR EL), he makes gems as a 
natural byproduct of his researches, worth between 1-3 gold per practice 
session.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  Your kingdom has attained skill level 5 in Psychic Magic.
At levels 5 and up, the usual 15% per level increase in the cast chance is 
discontinued, and the number of spells you can cast in Psychic Magic is 
capped at 3 Action, 2 Combat (however, skill level will still determine who 
attacks first in personal combat).  Instead, your characters of this exalted 
level are awarded a new Advanced Ability: 
  PSYCHIC MAGIC- "AUGUR COMBAT" SPELL (abbreviated "AC"):  The Psychic Mage 
performs a powerful augury (forecast), whereby he divines the probable 
outcome of the combat.  The computer will estimate the percentage chance of 
victory, if combat were to occur.  If the plan following the spell is a 
combat-oriented plan, then if the chances are too low for the character's 
courage, he will shirk combat (Coward 80%, Cautious 60%, Brave 40%, Berserk 
20%).  Any encounter plan can be stated after casting this spell.  Usually 
this spell should be the first tactic ordered, when it won't cost you a 
combat round; if it comes later, then the result will be an attempt to flee. 
Note: with old Saga programs, order this spell with "GI 32".


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  Your kingdom has reached skill level 5 in Illusions.  At 
levels 5 and up, the usual 15% per level increase in the cast chance is 
discontinued, and the number of spells you can cast in Illusions is capped 
at 3 Action, 2 Combat.  The effects of the "Mirror Image" and "Phantasmal 
Armies" spells are also capped at level 4 (however, skill level will still 
determine who attacks first in personal combat).  Instead, all characters of 
this high level gain a new Advanced Ability: 
  ILLUSORY MAGIC- "ILLUSORY HERO" SPELL (abbreviated "IH"):  By the wondrous 
magic power of this spell, the Illusionist creates an image of whatever 
Valhalla hero is currently in the world, to fight in his place.  It is 
similar to "Mirror-Image Phantasm", except that 15% is subtracted from the 
chance to disbelieve, and the illusory hero will usually not turn on its 
master if the illusion wins (unless the alignments of the illusion and the 
spellcaster are implacably hostile, for example Good versus Evil).  Note: 
with old Saga programs, order this spell with "GI 34".


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  Your kingdom has attained skill level 6 in Illusions.  
Your characters of this exalted level gain the following Advanced Ability: 
  ILLUSORY MAGIC- PLACES OF POWER:  The Illusionist can now use the magic of 
certain Illusory Places of Power to increase the success chance of spells.  
At any Maze, Labyrinth or Magic Pool, the success chance to cast an Illusory 
spell is increased by 20%.  For Search actions, the 20% bonus is applied 
when that type of feature is searched.  For Action spells, the bonus is 
applied if that feature type is in the same province as the character, and 
is not occupied by a monster.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have attained skill level 7 in Illusions.  Your 
characters of this high level gain a new Advanced Ability: 
  ILLUSORY MAGIC- ENHANCED INVISIBILITY:  The spell now includes some 
masking of the senses of smell and hearing, giving the Illusionist an 
additional plus 15% chance when Stealing.  Also, any attempt to Flee while 
Invisible will have a plus 30% chance to succeed.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have attained skill level 8 in Illusions.  Your 
characters of this exalted level gain a new Advanced Ability: 
  ILLUSORY MAGIC- "DETECT ILLUSIONS" TALENT:  This Talent constantly 
operates by itself, without having to cast a spell.  In combat, it gives the 
Illusionist a plus 25% chance to disbelieve a magical illusion.  Also, the 
Phantasmal Armies spell has only half its normal effect when the Illusionist 
is present at a battle on the opposite side.


END MOVES REPORT

